v 3
d 'DATAMAP': Describe and check data you can't share
d
d datamap writes privacy-safe Markdown documentation of Stata datasets:
d one table row per variable with its type, label, missing count (with
d each extended missing code) and values or statistics, classified
d automatically, with controls to exclude sensitive variables, suppress
d small cells and withhold exact dates, and a safe preset for output that
d goes to a coding agent. Several datasets get a linkage section. saving()
d writes the same facts as a variable-level metadata table.
d
d The package includes four commands:
d - datamap: Privacy-safe Markdown documentation of one or more datasets
d - dataprobe: Console QC profiling, expectation gates, snapshot and diff
d - dataqa: Session defaults and a structured QA ledger over dataprobe
d - datamvp: Missing-value pattern analysis (fork of mvpatterns)
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d Distribution-Date: 20261110
d License: MIT
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d
d KW: data management
d KW: documentation
d KW: codebook
d KW: privacy
d KW: metadata
d
